1
00:00:03,240 --> 00:00:05,410
弗里曼：触觉…
Touch...

2
00:00:06,340 --> 00:00:08,480
味觉…
Taste...

3
00:00:08,600 --> 00:00:10,640
视觉…
Sight...

4
00:00:10,760 --> 00:00:13,280
嗅觉…
Smell...

5
00:00:13,390 --> 00:00:16,060
听觉
Hearing.

6
00:00:16,270 --> 00:00:20,160
这些就是我们连接世界的感官
These are the senses that connect us to the world.

7
00:00:20,280 --> 00:00:23,310
然而有木有多过这五个感官的呢？
But are there more than five senses?

8
00:00:25,450 --> 00:00:28,900
研究人员正深入我们的大脑深处
Researchers are diving into hidden folds of our brains,

9
00:00:29,020 --> 00:00:34,410
探索盲人实际能看到的东西…
discovering that the blind can actually see...

10
00:00:34,520 --> 00:00:40,520
思想可以横空飞越…
That thoughts can fly across space...

11
00:00:40,740 --> 00:00:46,700
不知怎么的 我们可能有能力去感受未来
And that somehow,we might have the power to feel the future.

12
00:00:46,810 --> 00:00:49,500
有第六感么？
Is there a sixth sense?

13
00:00:49,510 --> 00:00:51,210
科学频道 - 穿越虫洞 2x05
Science.Channel - Through the Wormhole 2x05

14
00:00:51,220 --> 00:00:57,090
空间 时间 生命本身
Space,time,life itself.

15
00:00:59,490 --> 00:01:04,390
宇宙的秘密，尽在穿越虫洞
The secrets of the cosmos lie through the wormhole.

16
00:01:10,370 --> 00:01:16,970
有第六感么？
Is There A Sixth Sense?

17
00:01:17,820 --> 00:01:22,620
人的大脑是个真正了不起的器官
The human brain is a truly remarkable organ.

18
00:01:22,730 --> 00:01:24,980
其包含的神经细胞
It contains as many nerve cells

19
00:01:25,100 --> 00:01:27,620
多如银河系里的星星
as there are stars in the Milky Way.

20
00:01:27,730 --> 00:01:33,290
景象 声音 味道 发生在我们周围的世界里的一切
Sights,sounds,smells,anything happening in the world around us

21
00:01:33,410 --> 00:01:35,700
引发的活动波
triggers waves of activity

22
00:01:35,810 --> 00:01:40,300
脉动透过我们头脑里的这张大网
that ripple through this vast network in our heads.

23
00:01:40,420 --> 00:01:43,440
难道这个网络与世界的互动方式
Could this network interact with the world

24
00:01:43,550 --> 00:01:45,740
我们尚未明了？
in ways we don't yet understand?

25
00:01:45,850 --> 00:01:48,310
我们才刚开始看到
We are only just beginning to see

26
00:01:48,420 --> 00:01:51,280
这些细胞的真正本领
what these cells are really capable of.

27
00:01:51,390 --> 00:01:54,520
只要大脑依然是个谜
As long as the brain remains a mystery,

28
00:01:54,630 --> 00:01:58,790
第六感就不能归咎为迷信
the sixth sense cannot be written off as superstition.

29
00:01:58,900 --> 00:02:03,470
合乎科学 是完全有可能的
Scientifically,it's entirely possible.

30
00:02:06,680 --> 00:02:09,430
我过去通常是个好孩子
I was mostly a good kid.

31
00:02:09,550 --> 00:02:14,280
但偶尔 我也会出格
But every once in a while,I stepped out of line.

32
00:02:17,450 --> 00:02:21,160
不过即使背着身体…
But even with my back turned...

33
00:02:23,190 --> 00:02:25,790
…我都知道我被逮住了
...I knew when I'd been caught.

34
00:02:25,900 --> 00:02:28,190
我就是能够…
I could just...

35
00:02:28,300 --> 00:02:31,500
感觉到她指责的目光
feel her accusing stare.

36
00:02:32,670 --> 00:02:36,910
这就是第六感么？
Was this a sixth sense?

37
00:02:40,250 --> 00:02:43,740
在荷兰蒂尔堡大学
At Tilburg University in the Netherlands,

38
00:02:43,850 --> 00:02:45,070
比阿特丽斯.德杰尔德在研究
Beatrice de Gelder is researching

39
00:02:45,190 --> 00:02:47,710
人与人之间的情感交流
how emotions travel from person to person.

40
00:02:47,820 --> 00:02:51,190
她研究盲人的视觉…
She studies blind sight...

41
00:02:53,360 --> 00:02:57,590
有些盲人有一个奇怪现象
...A strange phenomenon in which some blind people

42
00:02:57,700 --> 00:03:01,790
就是能够看到别人的脸部情绪
are able to see emotions in other people's faces.

43
00:03:01,900 --> 00:03:04,840
德杰尔德：我们往往认为视觉感知
De Gelder:We send to think of visual perception

44
00:03:04,850 --> 00:03:06,740
是完好眼睛的问题
as a matter of intact eyes.

45
00:03:06,750 --> 00:03:08,230
事实上 眼睛只是看
In fact,the eyes only see

46
00:03:08,240 --> 00:03:11,100
因为它们连接到大脑
because they are connected to the brain.

47
00:03:11,210 --> 00:03:14,740
弗里曼：比阿特丽斯的大多数病人并没有表现出失明
Most of Beatrice's patients don't appear blind.

48
00:03:14,850 --> 00:03:18,340
从外表看 他们的眼睛看上去完全正常
On the outside,their eyes look perfectly normal.

49
00:03:18,460 --> 00:03:22,460
但是在里头 存在着暗伤
But on the inside,there is hidden damage.

50
00:03:24,460 --> 00:03:25,950
在健康的大脑里
In a healthy brain,

51
00:03:26,060 --> 00:03:29,820
复杂的信号交响乐从眼睛
a complex symphony of signals flows from the eyes

52
00:03:29,940 --> 00:03:32,890
传送到一个叫做视觉皮层的区域
to a region called the visual cortex.

53
00:03:33,010 --> 00:03:36,060
但若是视觉皮层遭到了损伤
But if the visual cortex gets damaged,

54
00:03:36,180 --> 00:03:38,530
通常是中风的后果
usually as a result of a stroke,

55
00:03:38,640 --> 00:03:41,740
信号就不再接收了
the signals can no longer be picked up.

56
00:03:41,850 --> 00:03:45,940
中风通常只影响皮层的一侧
A stroke normally affects only one side of the cortex,

57
00:03:46,050 --> 00:03:49,780
让患者失明一只眼睛
leaving the patient blind in one eye.

58
00:03:49,890 --> 00:03:51,610
比阿特丽斯着手研究
Beatrice is investigating

59
00:03:51,730 --> 00:03:54,520
大脑是否有其他办法
whether the brain might have other ways

60
00:03:54,630 --> 00:03:57,050
来获取那只眼睛传来的信号
to pick up signals from that eye.

61
00:03:57,160 --> 00:03:59,490
她利用隔断来分开
She uses a partition to separate

62
00:03:59,600 --> 00:04:03,730
患者的盲眼与好眼所看到的东西
what a patient's blind eye and functioning eye can see.

63
00:04:03,840 --> 00:04:08,830
电脑打出的图像有高兴 悲伤 愤怒的表情
A computer shows images of happy,sad,or angry faces

64
00:04:08,940 --> 00:04:10,310
只给一侧
to one side only.

65
00:04:12,310 --> 00:04:14,070
德杰尔德：我们给一个刺激
De Gelder:So,we present a stimulus.

66
00:04:14,180 --> 00:04:16,140
那个图像是有人在笑
It's an image of somebody laughing,

67
00:04:16,250 --> 00:04:17,370
有人在表达喜悦
somebody expressing joy.

68
00:04:17,490 --> 00:04:19,680
弗里曼：患者头部的电极
Electrodes on the patient's face

69
00:04:19,790 --> 00:04:21,740
会接收到他肌肉的抽搐
pick up any twitches of his muscles,

70
00:04:21,860 --> 00:04:26,530
检测他对屏幕上的情感如何反应
detecting if he reacts to the emotions on display.

71
00:04:27,920 --> 00:04:32,240
我们看到了他的脸居然在模仿
We see that his face was actually imitating.

72
00:04:32,360 --> 00:04:35,650
他在不知情的情况下使用同样的肌肉 当然
He was using the same muscles without knowing it,of course,

73
00:04:35,760 --> 00:04:38,280
他在屏幕上看到的模型
that the model he is seeing on the screen

74
00:04:38,390 --> 00:04:40,550
用来产生那个微笑
uses to produce that smile.

75
00:04:40,660 --> 00:04:45,550
弗里曼：引人瞩目的是那个情绪面孔
What's remarkable is that the emotional faces

76
00:04:45,670 --> 00:04:48,820
只是出现在患者的盲眼那一侧
are being shown only to the patient's blind side.

77
00:04:48,940 --> 00:04:52,660
好眼只能看到中性的表情
The seeing eye only sees neutral expressions.

78
00:04:52,770 --> 00:04:54,900
好 一遍又一遍
Yet,time and again,

79
00:04:55,010 --> 00:04:57,700
比阿特丽斯的患者模仿的情绪是
Beatrice's patients imitate the emotions

80
00:04:57,810 --> 00:04:59,700
他们的盲眼所看到的
their blind eye is looking at.

81
00:04:59,820 --> 00:05:05,510
不过反应并非全凭良心
But the response is not a conscience one.

82
00:05:05,620 --> 00:05:07,080
德杰尔德：我们问过他们
De Gelder:We asked the person,

83
00:05:07,190 --> 00:05:08,880
你肯定么 还是你蒙的？
"Were you sure,or are you guessing?"

84
00:05:08,990 --> 00:05:12,180
我们得到的系统答案是他们在蒙
And we systematically get the answer that they were guessing.

85
00:05:12,300 --> 00:05:16,350
弗里曼：比阿特丽斯认为盲视是深藏不露的
Beatrice believes blind sight is a deeply buried,

86
00:05:16,470 --> 00:05:18,420
潜意识的感官系统
subconscious sensory system

87
00:05:18,540 --> 00:05:20,360
根植于大脑的看不见的地方
rooted in a hidden part of the brain

88
00:05:20,470 --> 00:05:23,190
从眼睛接收信号
that receives signals from the eyes

89
00:05:23,310 --> 00:05:26,240
只出现在图像加载情绪时
only when the image is loaded with emotion.

90
00:05:28,810 --> 00:05:31,810
然而那部分大脑会在哪里呢？
But where could that part of the brain be?

91
00:05:32,950 --> 00:05:34,740
德杰尔德：我们在努力
De Gelder:We are really trying

92
00:05:34,850 --> 00:05:37,180
深入到大脑的各个层面
to tap into the different layers of the brain.

93
00:05:37,290 --> 00:05:38,610
从地表
From the surface landscape,

94
00:05:38,720 --> 00:05:40,880
我们试图深入到地下去
we try to sort of go underground in a way.

95
00:05:40,990 --> 00:05:42,650
你可以看到 这个就像是
You can see that this is,like,

96
00:05:42,760 --> 00:05:44,960
地下或地下工作
underground or undercover work.

97
00:05:45,960 --> 00:05:47,860
它都建立在什么上呢？
What is it all built on?

98
00:05:47,970 --> 00:05:49,790
那是较深 较古老的层面么？
What are the lower,more ancient layers?

99
00:05:49,900 --> 00:05:53,630
弗里曼：比阿特丽斯揭开了那些层面
Beatrice uncovered those layers

100
00:05:53,740 --> 00:05:56,360
通过将同样的面部表情图像演示给
by showing the same images of facial expressions

101
00:05:56,480 --> 00:06:00,770
失明的患者看 此时他们呆在核磁共振里
to blind-sight patients while they were inside an M.R.I.

102
00:06:00,880 --> 00:06:03,800
通常 眼睛的信息
Normally,information from the eyes

103
00:06:03,920 --> 00:06:08,510
通过视觉神经直接传送给视觉皮层
travels down the optic nerve directly to the visual cortex.

104
00:06:08,620 --> 00:06:11,810
不过当眼睛看到人的情感时
But when the eyes are looking at human emotions,

105
00:06:11,930 --> 00:06:14,310
信号会偏离路径
the signals diverge from that path

106
00:06:14,430 --> 00:06:17,850
传送给杏仁核 上丘
and travel to the amygdala,the superior colliculus,

107
00:06:17,960 --> 00:06:21,760
大脑里的六个别的结构
and six other structures in the brain.

108
00:06:21,870 --> 00:06:22,990
德杰尔德：人的视觉系统
De Gelder:The human visual system

109
00:06:23,100 --> 00:06:25,790
包括了至少九个不同的途径
consists at least of nine different pathways.

110
00:06:25,910 --> 00:06:28,730
其中只有一个我们开始有所了解
Only one of those we begin to understand,

111
00:06:28,840 --> 00:06:32,980
其它八个则完全情况不明
and the eight other ones are completely in the background.

112
00:06:34,410 --> 00:06:38,010
所以唯有这样 就是那个需要回避一下
So it's only in the case where that one needs to be sidestepped

113
00:06:38,120 --> 00:06:40,580
以使替代的途径有所机会
that the alternative pathways have a chance.

114
00:06:40,690 --> 00:06:46,220
弗里曼：比阿特丽斯已经找到潜意识的心理途径
Beatrice has identified subconscious mental pathways

115
00:06:46,330 --> 00:06:50,320
能让我们不用看到情感刺激
that allow us not to see emotional stimuli

116
00:06:50,430 --> 00:06:52,160
就能感受到它们
but to sense them.

117
00:06:52,270 --> 00:06:53,930
我们都有这些途径
We all have these pathways,

118
00:06:54,040 --> 00:06:56,660
即使它们通常
even though they are normally overwhelmed

119
00:06:56,770 --> 00:06:59,300
被我们的主要视觉搞得水泄不通
by our primary sense of sight.

120
00:06:59,410 --> 00:07:02,270
这是首个科学证据
It's the first scientific evidence

121
00:07:02,380 --> 00:07:05,040
有新的感觉超越了我们所知的五个.
of a new sense beyond the five we know.

122
00:07:05,150 --> 00:07:08,110
德杰尔德：人们应该洗耳恭听
De Gelder:One should have a sympathetic ear

123
00:07:08,220 --> 00:07:10,340
那些有关第六感的鼓噪
to those noises about a sixth sense

124
00:07:10,450 --> 00:07:12,010
因为我们对大脑的能力
because we don't have a clear view yet

125
00:07:12,120 --> 00:07:13,710
尚未有明确的说法
of the abilities of the brain.

126
00:07:13,820 --> 00:07:16,550
弗里曼：比阿特丽斯的研究已经表明
Beatrice's work has shown

127
00:07:16,660 --> 00:07:19,020
我们的大脑能够感知东西
that our brains can sense things

128
00:07:19,130 --> 00:07:21,920
甚至我们都不知晓它们
even when we are not aware of them.

129
00:07:22,030 --> 00:07:25,560
这意味着对第六感的任何搜索
It implies that any search for a sixth sense

130
00:07:25,670 --> 00:07:28,690
都取决于对自觉地意识与
depends on understanding the boundary

131
00:07:28,800 --> 00:07:33,270
潜意识经历之间的认识
between conscious awareness and subconscious experience.

132
00:07:37,740 --> 00:07:40,840
每月一次 有一群哲学家精英
Once a month,an elite group of philosophers

133
00:07:40,950 --> 00:07:44,950
相会于格林威治村的小酒馆里
meets at a small tavern in Greenwich Village.

134
00:07:47,820 --> 00:07:49,590
问候 纽约
Greetings,New York.

135
00:07:50,590 --> 00:07:51,750
弗里曼：他们自称是
They call themselves

136
00:07:51,860 --> 00:07:54,480
纽约意识共同体
the New York Consciousness Collective.

137
00:07:54,590 --> 00:07:57,350
我的动作跟你一样？
I act like you act?

138
00:07:57,460 --> 00:07:59,990
我做的事跟你一样？
I do what you do?

139
00:08:00,100 --> 00:08:05,160
弗里曼：这个摇滚演唱会的掌舵人是大卫.查默斯
At the helm of this jam session is David Chalmers.

140
00:08:05,270 --> 00:08:08,490
他可能永远都进不了麦迪逊广场花园
He may never fill Madison Square Garden,

141
00:08:08,610 --> 00:08:13,330
不过他的研究赢得了学术界里越来越多的粉丝
but his research is earning him a growing fan base in academia.

142
00:08:13,440 --> 00:08:15,230
他努力去理解
He's trying to understand

143
00:08:15,350 --> 00:08:19,400
意识的属性和极限
the nature and limits of consciousness.

144
00:08:19,520 --> 00:08:21,870
意识为何物？
? What consciousness is?

145
00:08:21,980 --> 00:08:25,470
我没有头绪？
? I ain't got a clue?

146
00:08:25,590 --> 00:08:28,680
意识堪称是世上最大的谜团
Consciousness is pretty well the biggest mystery in the world,

147
00:08:28,790 --> 00:08:31,580
究其原因 就在于它是个难题
and for these reasons,because it's such a hard problem,

148
00:08:31,690 --> 00:08:33,480
科学家往往将其置于一旁
scientists tended just to set it aside.

149
00:08:33,600 --> 00:08:35,180
科学是客观
Science is objective.

150
00:08:35,300 --> 00:08:37,350
意识是主观
Consciousness is subjective.

151
00:08:37,470 --> 00:08:39,660
它就在最近几十年 真的
It's just in the last couple of decades,really,

152
00:08:39,770 --> 00:08:41,660
科学家回过头来
that scientists have started coming back

153
00:08:41,770 --> 00:08:44,460
意识到它本身有权利作为一个问题
to consciousness as a problem in its own right.

154
00:08:44,570 --> 00:08:48,660
弗里曼：大卫认为认识意识之道
David believes the way to understand consciousness

155
00:08:48,780 --> 00:08:51,930
就是从层面上进行思考 -
is to think of it in layers --

156
00:08:52,050 --> 00:08:55,500
那些我们感官所搜集的数据所构成的层面
layers constructed from the data our senses are gathering.

157
00:08:55,620 --> 00:08:57,970
所以说 意识具有各种不同的层次
So,consciousness has all these different levels.

158
00:08:58,090 --> 00:09:00,210
首先 有主要的意识
First of all,there's primary consciousness.

159
00:09:00,320 --> 00:09:02,580
这就是你周围事物的意识
This is consciousness of the things around you.

160
00:09:02,690 --> 00:09:05,480
放眼出去 我可能看到有人 看到他们周围的事物
I look out,I might see someone and see what's around them.

161
00:09:05,590 --> 00:09:08,110
那是我第一层次的意识
That's my first level of consciousness.

162
00:09:08,230 --> 00:09:10,080
但一旦我停下折射
But then if I stop and reflect,

163
00:09:10,200 --> 00:09:12,820
我可以自觉我的意识
I could be conscious of my consciousness.

164
00:09:12,930 --> 00:09:16,060
我可以意识到自己在想什么
I can become conscious of what I'm thinking about.

165
00:09:16,170 --> 00:09:19,290
于是我们就感悟到了意识的内部
Then we've got consciousness within consciousness.

166
00:09:19,400 --> 00:09:20,560
如果我再次折射
If I reflect again,

167
00:09:20,670 --> 00:09:23,090
我就能够开始意识到事实上
I can start to be conscious of the fact

168
00:09:23,210 --> 00:09:25,630
我意识到了我的意识
that I'm conscious of my consciousness.

169
00:09:25,740 --> 00:09:29,800
于是你就有了意识里套意识
Then you get consciousness that contains consciousness

170
00:09:29,910 --> 00:09:31,370
再套意识
that contains consciousness.

171
00:09:31,480 --> 00:09:32,600
进入了三个层次的深度
Go three levels deep.

172
00:09:32,710 --> 00:09:37,640
原则上 你可以将此重复至无穷
In principle,you could repeat this to infinity.

173
00:09:37,750 --> 00:09:41,640
弗里曼：由于我们的大脑要应对如此多的层次
Since our brain is dealing with so many layers,

174
00:09:41,760 --> 00:09:45,480
按理说 我们可能永远都掌握不了
it stands to reason that we might not always be aware

175
00:09:45,590 --> 00:09:47,520
我们所感受的一切
of everything we're sensing.

176
00:09:47,630 --> 00:09:50,420
查默斯：有些东西就是躲在
Some things are in the background

177
00:09:50,530 --> 00:09:51,920
你的意识里
of your consciousness,

178
00:09:52,030 --> 00:09:55,120
深藏不露
way out in the distance.

179
00:09:55,240 --> 00:09:58,390
有些东西在你的意识里忽隐忽现
Some things are flickering through your consciousness

180
00:09:58,510 --> 00:10:04,100
抓住你的注意片刻 然后就过了
that grab your attention for a moment,then they move on.

181
00:10:04,210 --> 00:10:08,000
有些东西成了你意识的重点
Some things are in the focus of your consciousness.

182
00:10:08,110 --> 00:10:09,970
它们抓住了你的关注
They grab your attention.

183
00:10:10,080 --> 00:10:11,470
它们并不松手
They don't let go.

184
00:10:11,590 --> 00:10:14,940
弗里曼：但我们如何发现我们错过了什么？
But how do we discover what we are missing?

185
00:10:15,060 --> 00:10:19,180
为什么只有特定的神经活动
Why does only certain neural activity

186
00:10:19,290 --> 00:10:22,150
能设法争取进入我们的意识呢？
manage to fight its way into our awareness?

187
00:10:22,260 --> 00:10:24,890
我们意识到某些事物时
What's actually happening in our brains

188
00:10:25,000 --> 00:10:26,950
大脑里所发生的情况
when we are conscious of something

189
00:10:27,070 --> 00:10:30,190
仍然整个是个谜团
is still a complete mystery.

190
00:10:30,300 --> 00:10:32,860
关于意识的一个基本问题
One of the basic questions about consciousness

191
00:10:32,970 --> 00:10:36,200
就是你能否从物理过程来解释它
is whether you can explain it in terms of physical processes

192
00:10:36,310 --> 00:10:38,770
因为我们已经习惯了科学上的概念
'cause we've got used to the idea in science

193
00:10:38,880 --> 00:10:41,300
那是你从一些基础的物理学开始的
that you start with a few basics in physics,

194
00:10:41,410 --> 00:10:42,970
比如空间 时间和物质
like space and time and matter.

195
00:10:43,080 --> 00:10:45,470
把它们放在一起 你就可以解释一切了
Put them together,you can explain everything else.

196
00:10:45,580 --> 00:10:46,770
你可以解释化学
You can explain chemistry.

197
00:10:46,890 --> 00:10:48,010
你可以解释生物学
You can explain biology.

198
00:10:48,120 --> 00:10:50,140
现在 我觉得就意识而言
Now,I think in the case of consciousness,

199
00:10:50,250 --> 00:10:52,340
这一大串解释将完蛋了
this great chain of explanation breaks down.

200
00:10:52,460 --> 00:10:55,280
我的看法是 我们在意识的属性上
My view is,we've got a new fundamental building block

201
00:10:55,390 --> 00:10:56,710
有了新的基本模块
in nature of consciousness,

202
00:10:56,830 --> 00:11:01,060
我们需要了解掌控它的基本规律
and we need to understand the fundamental laws that govern it.

203
00:11:02,460 --> 00:11:04,820
弗里曼：这位科学家认为他发现了
This scientist thinks he's discovered

204
00:11:04,940 --> 00:11:09,660
意识惊人的新模样
a new and surprising aspect of consciousness.

205
00:11:09,770 --> 00:11:13,270
他认为它不只是存在于我们的头脑里
He believes it does not simply exist within our minds

206
00:11:13,380 --> 00:11:16,230
而且还向外延伸
but extends outward,as well.

207
00:11:16,350 --> 00:11:21,220
他声称他有证据来证明它
And he claims he has the evidence to prove it.

208
00:11:24,350 --> 00:11:26,590
思想是什么？
What is a thought?

209
00:11:27,160 --> 00:11:28,620
神经学家会说
Neuroscientists would say

210
00:11:28,740 --> 00:11:32,740
它只是我们大脑里电活动的一种形式
it's just a pattern of electrical activity inside our brains.

211
00:11:32,850 --> 00:11:38,140
但若是我发怒或微笑 我的思想就能够穿过房间
But if I scowl or smile,my thoughts can cross a room.

212
00:11:38,260 --> 00:11:41,950
事实上 它们在这当口就让你触手可及
In fact,they're reaching out to touch you right now.

213
00:11:42,060 --> 00:11:46,180
有些科学家认为这就是第六感在起作用 -
Some scientists believe this is how the sixth sense works --

214
00:11:46,300 --> 00:11:50,260
人的思想融入了
that human thoughts merge into a collective consciousness

215
00:11:50,370 --> 00:11:53,040
遍及全球的集体意识
that spans the globe.

216
00:11:55,040 --> 00:11:59,970
罗杰.尼尔森花了30年时光
Roger Nelson has spent the past 30 years

217
00:12:00,080 --> 00:12:03,270
来寻找全球意识的证据
looking for evidence of a global mind.

218
00:12:03,380 --> 00:12:06,740
尼尔森：意识就存在于现实世界里
Consciousness lives in the real world.

219
00:12:06,850 --> 00:12:08,270
接触微不足道
The touch is very light.

220
00:12:08,390 --> 00:12:10,440
但其真正接触的程度
But to the degree that it's a real touch,

221
00:12:10,560 --> 00:12:11,850
却是极其重要的
it's extremely important.

222
00:12:11,960 --> 00:12:14,950
大多数人并不相信这是有可能的
Most people don't believe this is possible.

223
00:12:15,060 --> 00:12:19,390
研究表明这是有可能的
The research shows that it is possible.

224
00:12:19,500 --> 00:12:22,460
弗里曼：在上世纪80年代中期 罗杰着手调查
In the mid-1980s,Roger began investigating

225
00:12:22,570 --> 00:12:23,930
一个奇怪的现象
a strange phenomenon

226
00:12:24,040 --> 00:12:27,460
已经有几位研究者报告了
that had been reported by several other researchers.

227
00:12:27,570 --> 00:12:31,330
他们注意到那种叫做随机数字发生器的
They had noticed that the readouts of electronic devices

228
00:12:31,440 --> 00:12:33,470
电子设备的读数
called random-number generators

229
00:12:33,580 --> 00:12:36,870
可以会受到坐在其旁边的人的影响
could be affected by people sitting next to them

230
00:12:36,980 --> 00:12:41,110
若是那人全神贯注于它们的话
if those people focused their thoughts on them.

231
00:12:41,220 --> 00:12:43,910
在多年的长期实验过程中
In the course of a long series of experiments over years,

232
00:12:44,020 --> 00:12:46,250
我们发现人们可以改变
we found that people could change the behavior

233
00:12:46,360 --> 00:12:48,050
这些随机数字发生器的举动
of these random-number generators

234
00:12:48,160 --> 00:12:51,790
非常轻微却非常显著
very slightly but significantly.

235
00:12:51,900 --> 00:12:55,620
弗里曼：随机数字发生器就是电子抛硬币
Random-number generators are electronic coin tosses.

236
00:12:55,740 --> 00:12:58,030
取代正反面
Instead of heads or tails,

237
00:12:58,140 --> 00:13:01,860
它们掷出的数目或零
they throw ones or zeros.

238
00:13:01,980 --> 00:13:06,430
其结果全凭随机
Their results are supposed to be totally random.

239
00:13:06,550 --> 00:13:10,300
罗杰认为如果有人呆在其旁边
Roger reasoned that if one person sitting close by

240
00:13:10,420 --> 00:13:12,310
可以改变其读数的话
could alter their readouts,

241
00:13:12,420 --> 00:13:15,770
那么没准全体老百姓的想法
then perhaps the mass thoughts of entire cities

242
00:13:15,890 --> 00:13:17,210
可以达到同样的效果
could do the same.

243
00:13:17,320 --> 00:13:21,150
世界各地的随机数字发生器能够
Could random-number generators placed around the world

244
00:13:21,260 --> 00:13:25,080
用来跟踪芸芸众生的头脑么？
be used to track the minds of millions of individuals?

245
00:13:25,200 --> 00:13:29,160
尼尔森：我们所做的就是开展一个科学实验
What we have done is set up a scientific experiment

246
00:13:29,270 --> 00:13:31,360
其具有极其简单的假设
with a fairly simple hypothesis.

247
00:13:31,470 --> 00:13:32,760
想法是
The idea is,

248
00:13:32,870 --> 00:13:36,360
当有大量的人共享一个意识形态
when large numbers of people share a consciousness state,

249
00:13:36,480 --> 00:13:37,760
尤其是情感
especially emotional,

250
00:13:37,880 --> 00:13:41,870
那么我们的网络将显示出偏离随机性
then our network will show deviations from randomness.

251
00:13:41,980 --> 00:13:43,970
弗里曼：到了上世纪末
By the late 1990s,

252
00:13:44,080 --> 00:13:47,740
罗杰说服了世界上几位同僚
Roger had persuaded several colleagues across the globe

253
00:13:47,850 --> 00:13:51,450
收集他们实验室里的随机数字数据
to collect random-number data in their labs.

254
00:13:51,560 --> 00:13:55,010
全球意识项目应运而生了
The global consciousness project was born.

255
00:13:55,130 --> 00:13:56,280
这是地图
This is a map

256
00:13:56,400 --> 00:13:58,680
表明全球意识项目
that shows where the global consciousness project

257
00:13:58,800 --> 00:14:02,190
已遍布世界各地
has installations all around the world.

258
00:14:02,300 --> 00:14:06,060
有夏威夷 澳大利亚 新西兰
That's Hawaii there,Australia,New Zealand,

259
00:14:06,170 --> 00:14:08,090
它们很多在欧洲
lots of them in Europe.

260
00:14:08,210 --> 00:14:11,430
有随机事件发生器或随机数字发生器
There's a random-event generator or a random-number generator

261
00:14:11,540 --> 00:14:14,170
连接到其中每一个地方的计算机上
attached to a computer at each of those places.

262
00:14:14,280 --> 00:14:17,340
弗里曼：这个全球网络全天候工作
This global network runs 24/7,

263
00:14:17,450 --> 00:14:21,380
收集数据并将其发送至
collecting data and then sending it back to a server

264
00:14:21,490 --> 00:14:24,050
普林斯顿罗杰的实验室的服务器上
at Roger's lab in Princeton.

265
00:14:24,160 --> 00:14:26,650
尼尔森：我们获取实时数据
We take the real-time data,

266
00:14:26,760 --> 00:14:30,820
每一秒钟 都会有色块呈现出来
and every second,a color block will appear.

267
00:14:30,930 --> 00:14:32,620
通常都是很小的
Mostly it's small,

268
00:14:32,730 --> 00:14:37,060
不过一旦有像这样的数据上较大的偏差…
but when there's a big deviation in the data like that...

269
00:14:37,170 --> 00:14:40,170
噢 天哪 又一个
Oh,my God,another one.

270
00:14:41,340 --> 00:14:44,030
通常不易看到这么大的偏差
This is unusual to see so many large deviations

271
00:14:44,150 --> 00:14:45,470
在这么短的时间里.
in such a short time.

272
00:14:45,580 --> 00:14:49,410
弗里曼：每逢有重大的全球性事件
Every time there was a major global event,

273
00:14:49,520 --> 00:14:53,640
罗杰都会细察其网络是否偏离正常值
Roger checks to see if his network deviates from normal.

274
00:14:53,760 --> 00:14:55,550
许多回 确实是这样
And many times,it does.

275
00:14:55,660 --> 00:14:57,780
一些最强的变化
Some of the strongest changes

276
00:14:57,890 --> 00:15:02,330
就发生在2008年的总统选举期间
took place during the presidential elections of 2008.

277
00:15:04,470 --> 00:15:06,660
尼尔森：投票结束时
When the polls closed,

278
00:15:06,770 --> 00:15:10,260
媒体宣称 看来奥巴马胜出了
the media were saying,"Looks like Obama has won."

279
00:15:10,370 --> 00:15:12,230
这个图表显示的数据
This graph shows the data

280
00:15:12,340 --> 00:15:16,400
是投票结束后接下来的5个小时
from the time the polls closed for the next five hours.

281
00:15:16,510 --> 00:15:18,580
其中央是奥巴马的胜选演讲
In the middle of that is Obama's victory speech.

282
00:15:20,720 --> 00:15:23,940
我们从来就不是乌合之众
We have never been just a collection of individuals.

283
00:15:24,050 --> 00:15:28,990
我们是并始终是美利坚合众国
We are and always will be the United States of America.

284
00:15:32,630 --> 00:15:34,880
尼尔森：那是个很强的走势
This is a strong trend.

285
00:15:35,000 --> 00:15:36,930
它一路上升
It just goes straight up this incline.

286
00:15:38,270 --> 00:15:39,790
这就像是1000比1的机遇
It's like 1,000-to-1 odds

287
00:15:39,900 --> 00:15:43,360
我们应该会有那种积极影响的累积
that we should have that accumulation of positive effects

288
00:15:43,470 --> 00:15:44,710
在此种数据集里
in a data set this size.

289
00:15:46,780 --> 00:15:51,300
我们有超过340个独立的实验
We have more than 340 independent experiments.

290
00:15:51,410 --> 00:15:53,200
当我们将所有的数据放在一块
When we put all the data together

291
00:15:53,320 --> 00:15:56,070
12年试验所产生的
from 12 years of these experiments,

292
00:15:56,180 --> 00:15:57,610
最终的结果
the bottom-line result

293
00:15:57,720 --> 00:16:00,720
是10亿比1的机会
has odds against chance of a billion to one.

294
00:16:06,860 --> 00:16:09,020
弗里曼：罗杰的数据表明
Roger's data suggests

295
00:16:09,130 --> 00:16:12,020
存在有某种全球意识
there is some form of global consciousness.

296
00:16:12,130 --> 00:16:15,270
然而它有可能产生实际效果么？
But how might it actually work?

297
00:16:17,170 --> 00:16:19,360
生物学家鲁珀特.谢德瑞克
Biologist Rupert Sheldrake

298
00:16:19,470 --> 00:16:22,930
认为答案就在一个隐蔽的场里
believes the answer lies in a hidden field

299
00:16:23,040 --> 00:16:25,200
其产生于所有的生物
generated by all living things.

300
00:16:25,310 --> 00:16:28,820
他将其称之为形态场
He calls it a morphic field.

301
00:16:31,490 --> 00:16:33,410
场是影响的区域
Fields are regions of influence.

302
00:16:33,520 --> 00:16:37,950
不难看到磁场带来的场
It's easier to see what fields are with magnetic fields.

303
00:16:38,060 --> 00:16:40,920
这些球是小磁体
These balls are little magnets,

304
00:16:41,030 --> 00:16:44,020
我将它们落到盘子里
and as I drop them onto the plate,

305
00:16:44,130 --> 00:16:47,120
球就会相互吸引或排斥
the balls attract each other or repel each other.

306
00:16:47,240 --> 00:16:50,430
它们会转动 它们会结合在一起形成图案
They turn around,and so they all join up in patterns.

307
00:16:50,540 --> 00:16:52,500
场里存在着自我组织的性质
There's a self-organizing property in fields.

308
00:16:52,610 --> 00:16:55,770
它们是天生一体化的
They're inherently integrative.

309
00:16:55,880 --> 00:16:57,270
我所认为的是
And what I'm suggesting

310
00:16:57,380 --> 00:16:59,800
存在有另一种场 叫做形态场
is that there's another kind of field called morphic fields,

311
00:16:59,920 --> 00:17:02,840
其构成了动物和植物的形态
which organize the bodies of animals and plants

312
00:17:02,950 --> 00:17:06,480
构成了大脑和思想的活动
and organize the activities of brains and minds.

313
00:17:06,590 --> 00:17:09,880
弗里曼：鲁珀特认为就是形态场
Rupert believes that morphic fields

314
00:17:09,990 --> 00:17:13,580
让鸟类以完美的队形飞翔
are what allow birds to fly in perfect formation,

315
00:17:13,700 --> 00:17:17,290
指引群居动物大规模迁徙
what guide the mass migrations of herd animals,

316
00:17:17,400 --> 00:17:19,790
他同时认为
and he also believes

317
00:17:19,900 --> 00:17:22,760
它们就是我们会不可思议地感觉到
they are the reason we get that uncanny feeling

318
00:17:22,870 --> 00:17:24,610
有人在盯着我们的原因所在
when someone stares at us.

319
00:17:27,610 --> 00:17:30,900
他甚至进行了一系列的实验
He has even run a series of experiments

320
00:17:31,020 --> 00:17:34,620
试图证明这种感觉是真实的
to try to prove that this sense is real.

321
00:17:36,090 --> 00:17:38,890
没在看
Not looking.

322
00:17:40,460 --> 00:17:42,310
不管你在看或不在看
You either look or you don't look

323
00:17:42,430 --> 00:17:44,980
对别人随机的试验
in a random sequence of trials at somebody else,

324
00:17:45,100 --> 00:17:47,080
他们都得猜测每次试验
and they have to guess in each trial

325
00:17:47,200 --> 00:17:49,120
不管他们是否被盯着
if they're being stared at or not.

326
00:17:49,230 --> 00:17:52,660
没在看
Not looking.

327
00:17:52,770 --> 00:17:54,690
谢德瑞克：发令员应该集中注意力
The starer should concentrate their mind

328
00:17:54,810 --> 00:17:56,960
于他们所关注的人
on the person they're looking at.

329
00:17:57,080 --> 00:17:59,400
我做的时候 同时会想那人的名字
When I do it,I also think of the person's name.

330
00:17:59,510 --> 00:18:00,770
在看
Looking.

331
00:18:00,880 --> 00:18:03,200
我全神贯注于他们
I concentrate all my attention on them.

332
00:18:03,320 --> 00:18:05,500
我不看他们时
When I'm not looking at them,

333
00:18:05,620 --> 00:18:08,770
我会看着地板 或闭上我的眼睛
I look at the floor or I close my eyes,

334
00:18:08,890 --> 00:18:11,410
我会想完全不搭界的东西
and I think of something completely different.

335
00:18:11,520 --> 00:18:13,810
没在看
Not looking.

336
00:18:13,930 --> 00:18:15,480
好极了
Brilliant.

337
00:18:15,590 --> 00:18:18,350
14次对 6次错
14 right and 6 wrong.

338
00:18:18,460 --> 00:18:21,550
事情还在继续
Something's going on,

339
00:18:21,670 --> 00:18:23,950
尽管效果不大 但它是一贯的
and although the effect's not big,it's consistent

340
00:18:24,070 --> 00:18:27,160
重复了大量的试验
and it's repeated over large numbers of trials.

341
00:18:27,270 --> 00:18:31,130
弗里曼：鲁珀特收集了一堆证据
Rupert has gathered a body of evidence

342
00:18:31,240 --> 00:18:33,100
表明人们确实表现出能知道
that shows people really do appear to know

343
00:18:33,210 --> 00:18:34,900
他们被人盯着了
when they are being stared at.

344
00:18:35,010 --> 00:18:37,970
对他来说 这支持了其想法
For him,it supports the idea

345
00:18:38,080 --> 00:18:40,570
即我们的身体的周遭是形态场
that our bodies are surrounded by morphic fields,

346
00:18:40,690 --> 00:18:44,840
是我们自身的无形延伸
an invisible extension of ourselves.

347
00:18:44,960 --> 00:18:46,080
我所认为的是
What I'm suggesting

348
00:18:46,190 --> 00:18:48,580
我们的思想活动通过延伸的场
is that our minds work through extended fields

349
00:18:48,690 --> 00:18:52,020
远远超越了我们的大脑 进入了我们周围的世界
that stretch out far beyond our heads into the world around us,

350
00:18:52,130 --> 00:18:56,220
把我们与其他人以及我们的环境联系在了一起
linking us to other people and to our environment.

351
00:18:56,330 --> 00:19:00,430
弗里曼：许多科学家对鲁珀特的想法不屑一顾
Many scientists dismiss Rupert's ideas,

352
00:19:00,540 --> 00:19:03,900
认为如果有形态场的存在
arguing that if morphic fields exist,

353
00:19:04,010 --> 00:19:06,830
我们到现在就应该发现它们了
we should have detected them by now.

354
00:19:06,940 --> 00:19:10,500
不过在安大略省萨德伯里的一个昏暗的实验室里
But in a darkened lab in Sudbury,Ontario,

355
00:19:10,620 --> 00:19:12,670
这位研究人员认为他已经发现
this researcher believes he has

356
00:19:12,790 --> 00:19:14,840
并已经证明了
and that he has evidence

357
00:19:14,950 --> 00:19:19,360
思想可以从一个人的头脑飞到另一个人的头脑里
that thoughts can fly from one mind to another.

358
00:19:23,110 --> 00:19:25,130
每时每刻
Every minute of every day,

359
00:19:25,250 --> 00:19:28,500
我们都被一种无形的力量包围着
we are surrounded by an invisible force.

360
00:19:28,620 --> 00:19:34,110
我们的世界包裹在磁场里
Our world is wrapped in a magnetic field.

361
00:19:34,220 --> 00:19:36,280
对于地球上的许多生物而言
For many creatures on Earth,

362
00:19:36,390 --> 00:19:39,180
生命离了它将不复存在
life would be impossible without it.

363
00:19:39,290 --> 00:19:44,350
鸟类 海龟 鱼类依靠这个全球磁场
Birds,sea turtles,and fish rely on this global magnetism

364
00:19:44,470 --> 00:19:45,650
来导航
to navigate.

365
00:19:45,770 --> 00:19:49,520
我们的大脑也能够利用它么？
Could our minds be using it,too?

366
00:19:49,640 --> 00:19:54,670
或许它就是第六感的根源么？
And is it,perhaps,the root of the sixth sense?

367
00:19:56,580 --> 00:20:00,770
迈克尔.伯辛格执掌着加拿大劳伦森大学的
Michael Persinger runs the neuroscience research group

368
00:20:00,880 --> 00:20:04,540
神经科学研究组
at Laurentian University in Canada.

369
00:20:04,650 --> 00:20:08,480
地球磁场对动物的强大影响
The powerful effect of Earth's magnetic field on animals

370
00:20:08,590 --> 00:20:10,410
启发了他去调查
inspired him to investigate

371
00:20:10,530 --> 00:20:13,880
它是否也影响我们呢
whether it could also influence us.

372
00:20:14,000 --> 00:20:16,180
动物能够利用
Animals can use the three-dimensional magnetic field

373
00:20:16,290 --> 00:20:17,290
地球的三维磁场
of the Earth

374
00:20:17,410 --> 00:20:21,060
作为一种导航或归家的装备
as a kind of navigation or homing device.

375
00:20:21,170 --> 00:20:23,060
对此已经有很好的证据了
There's very good evidence for it.

376
00:20:23,170 --> 00:20:26,330
弗里曼：迈克尔所认为的可能存在于
The connection Michael suggests could exist

377
00:20:26,440 --> 00:20:29,330
地球磁场与人脑之间的联系
between Earth's magnetic field and human brains

378
00:20:29,450 --> 00:20:31,370
是极具争议的
is much more controversial.

379
00:20:31,480 --> 00:20:33,100
伯辛格：第六感实际上
The sixth sense is effectively

380
00:20:33,220 --> 00:20:36,010
就是发现远距离信息的能力 -
the ability to detect information at a distance --

381
00:20:36,120 --> 00:20:38,010
那是定义之一 -
that's one of the definitions --

382
00:20:38,120 --> 00:20:40,080
尽管其机制至今尚未知晓
through mechanisms not known to date.

383
00:20:40,190 --> 00:20:42,460
关键问题在于 它是如何做到的？
The critical question is,how is it done?

384
00:20:44,190 --> 00:20:45,980
地球的磁场
The magnetic field of the Earth

385
00:20:46,100 --> 00:20:49,520
本质上是种介质 我们全都暴露在其中
is basically the medium within which we were all exposed,

386
00:20:49,630 --> 00:20:51,160
我们70亿人
all 7 billion of us.

387
00:20:52,300 --> 00:20:53,760
就是它保证了
And that's what allows

388
00:20:53,870 --> 00:20:56,520
潜在的信息交流
the potential exchange of information.

389
00:20:56,640 --> 00:20:58,960
弗里曼：根据这个理论
According to this theory,

390
00:20:59,070 --> 00:21:02,900
地球的磁场就像是大海的波涛
Earth's magnetic field is like an ocean rippling with waves.

391
00:21:03,010 --> 00:21:05,570
我们大脑的电活动
Electrical activity from our brains

392
00:21:05,680 --> 00:21:07,570
能够处在风口浪尖
can surf along on top of it,

393
00:21:07,680 --> 00:21:10,240
从一个人传递给另一个人
passing from one person to another.

394
00:21:10,350 --> 00:21:13,710
这是个激进的想法
It's a radical idea,

395
00:21:13,820 --> 00:21:16,310
不过迈克尔设计了一个精心的实验
but Michael has designed an elaborate experiment

396
00:21:16,430 --> 00:21:19,480
来对此进行测试
to put it to the test.

397
00:21:19,600 --> 00:21:22,020
无论如何 你都别钻到他的脑袋里去
And whatever you do,don't drill into his head.

398
00:21:22,130 --> 00:21:23,920
环钻术在加拿大是不合法的
Trephining is outlawed in Canada.

399
00:21:24,030 --> 00:21:30,030
他的研究小组安排了两个课题 曼迪和马克
His team placed two subjects,Mandy and Mark,

400
00:21:30,240 --> 00:21:32,600
分别在相距20英尺的房间里
in rooms 20 feet apart.

401
00:21:32,710 --> 00:21:35,030
房间相互之间是
The rooms are acoustically and visually isolated

402
00:21:35,140 --> 00:21:37,100
声光隔离的
from one another.

403
00:21:37,210 --> 00:21:39,700
他们还完全屏蔽掉
They are also completely shielded

404
00:21:39,820 --> 00:21:41,770
地球的磁场
from Earth's magnetic field.

405
00:21:41,880 --> 00:21:43,410
迈克尔换上了
Michael replaces that

406
00:21:43,520 --> 00:21:48,680
精心控制的磁场 由他亲自设计的
with a precisely controlled magnetic field of his own design

407
00:21:48,790 --> 00:21:52,280
产生于这个头戴的电子线圈
generated by electrical coils on this headband.

408
00:21:52,390 --> 00:21:55,020
如此一来 他就能够确保
In this way,he can be sure

409
00:21:55,130 --> 00:21:59,990
曼迪和马克经受到完全相同的磁场
that Mandy and Mark experience identical magnetic fields.

410
00:22:00,100 --> 00:22:02,790
通过对相距一段距离的
By producing the same complex configuration

411
00:22:02,900 --> 00:22:05,330
两个不同的大脑
of a magnetic field in two different brains

412
00:22:05,440 --> 00:22:06,590
产生同样复杂编排的磁场
at a distance,

413
00:22:06,710 --> 00:22:09,130
你基本上模仿的是
you're basically imitating what happens in nature

414
00:22:09,240 --> 00:22:10,670
地球磁场实际情况
in the Earth's magnetic field.

415
00:22:10,780 --> 00:22:12,570
我要关灯了
I'm going to turn off the lights,

416
00:22:12,680 --> 00:22:15,310
我将全程记录你的脑电图
and I'll be recording your E.E.G. the entire time.

417
00:22:19,320 --> 00:22:22,510
我们的确将能够看到他们的脑活动
And we'll be able to see if,indeed,their brain activity

418
00:22:22,620 --> 00:22:26,520
是否相同 一旦他们分享同样的磁场的话
is the same once they share the same magnetic field.

419
00:22:28,230 --> 00:22:30,350
弗里曼：在接下来的20分钟里
Over the course of the next 20 minutes,

420
00:22:30,460 --> 00:22:33,620
马克那里的灯将闪烁几次
a light will flash at Mark several times

421
00:22:33,730 --> 00:22:37,790
期间曼迪在其黑暗的房间里不受干扰
while Mandy remains undisturbed in her darkened room.

422
00:22:37,900 --> 00:22:39,460
迈克尔和他的小组
Michael and his team

423
00:22:39,570 --> 00:22:42,030
监视着他俩的大脑活动
monitor both of their brains' activity.

424
00:22:42,140 --> 00:22:46,630
三分钟后 马克房间里的灯
Three minutes in,the light begins to flash

425
00:22:46,750 --> 00:22:48,670
开始闪烁
in Mark's room.

426
00:22:48,780 --> 00:22:50,340
你可以看到一个峰值出现在那里
You can see a nice spike right there.

427
00:22:50,450 --> 00:22:52,340
约5分钟后
About five minutes later,

428
00:22:52,450 --> 00:22:54,970
灯光再次闪烁
the light flashes again.

429
00:22:55,090 --> 00:22:57,540
同样的强度 其实 甚至对这个人 你都可以看到峰值
Same intensity. Actually,you can see the spikes even in this one.

430
00:22:57,660 --> 00:22:59,810
曼迪的脑活动的飙升
Mandy's brain activity

431
00:22:59,930 --> 00:23:03,960
恰好就是马克看到闪烁的灯光的时候
spiked right at the time mark saw the flashing light.

432
00:23:06,930 --> 00:23:09,920
现在伯辛格博士的小组需要知道
Now Dr. Persinger's team need to know

433
00:23:10,030 --> 00:23:13,860
曼迪在她坐在暗房里的感受
what Mandy experienced while she sat in the dark.

434
00:23:13,970 --> 00:23:17,360
曼迪：约三分钟时
Well,at about three minutes in,

435
00:23:17,470 --> 00:23:21,700
在我的左眼的左侧
in my left visual field of my left eye,

436
00:23:21,810 --> 00:23:24,770
我感受到了闪光
I experienced a bright flash.

437
00:23:24,880 --> 00:23:26,670
它很短暂
And it lasted very briefly,

438
00:23:26,790 --> 00:23:30,910
其感觉就好像是再次消逝在黑暗中
and it felt like it just sort of faded into the darkness again.

439
00:23:31,020 --> 00:23:34,910
在约6到8分钟后
Later on at around six to eight minutes in,

440
00:23:35,030 --> 00:23:37,250
我看到有闪光在我的右侧
I had a flash in my right peripheral field.

441
00:23:37,360 --> 00:23:39,720
伯辛格：在灯光对一个人闪烁时
When the light was flashing to one,

442
00:23:39,830 --> 00:23:40,950
产生了所有这些变化
producing all these changes,

443
00:23:41,070 --> 00:23:42,520
另一个人的大脑活动
the other person's brain activity,

444
00:23:42,630 --> 00:23:43,680
即使他们处在暗处
even though they were in the dark,

445
00:23:43,800 --> 00:23:44,800
同样也发生了变化
also changed.

446
00:23:44,910 --> 00:23:48,690
弗里曼：实验似乎表明
The experiment seems to show

447
00:23:48,810 --> 00:23:51,700
不同地点的两个大脑
that two brains in separate locations

448
00:23:51,810 --> 00:23:53,630
可以共享一个经历
can share a single experience.

449
00:23:53,750 --> 00:23:56,740
伯辛格：人的思想并不是非物理的
Human thoughts are not non-physical.

450
00:23:56,850 --> 00:23:59,670
它们是动作电位的物理单元
They are physical units of action potentials

451
00:23:59,780 --> 00:24:01,640
出自神经本身
from the nerve itself.

452
00:24:01,750 --> 00:24:03,280
它们能跨越空间传送么？
Can they be transmitted across space?

453
00:24:03,390 --> 00:24:04,940
在某种条件下 绝对可以
Under certain conditions,absolutely,

454
00:24:05,060 --> 00:24:06,110
对此是有证据的
and there's evidence for it.

455
00:24:06,220 --> 00:24:08,950
如果我们有70亿个人脑
If we have seven billion human brains

456
00:24:09,060 --> 00:24:11,120
全都沉没于磁场中 这样它们就
all immersed in the magnetic field,which they are,

457
00:24:11,230 --> 00:24:12,980
一个发生变化 如果它是联系的 -
then a change in one,if it's connected --

458
00:24:13,100 --> 00:24:15,120
我们因为有磁力线
and we are 'cause the magnetic flux lines

459
00:24:15,230 --> 00:24:17,550
正好经过我们 正好经过我们的大脑 -
go right through us,right through our brains --

460
00:24:17,670 --> 00:24:20,200
于是一个人的变化就能影响到每一个人
then a change in one could influence everyone.

461
00:24:22,610 --> 00:24:26,360
迈克尔.伯辛格认为他已经证明了
Michael Persinger believes he has evidence

462
00:24:26,480 --> 00:24:29,430
第六感的原始形态 -
for a primitive form of sixth sense --

463
00:24:29,550 --> 00:24:32,400
能够分享
an ability to share simple sensations

464
00:24:32,520 --> 00:24:35,370
远离我们的人的简单感觉
with people who are far away from us.

465
00:24:35,490 --> 00:24:39,780
不过我们的感觉或许不光能穿越空间
But our senses may not just be able to travel across space.

466
00:24:39,890 --> 00:24:43,020
它们或许能够穿越时间
They may be able to reach out across time

467
00:24:43,130 --> 00:24:45,330
感觉到未来
and feel the future.

468
00:24:47,950 --> 00:24:53,120
科学全都是似乎难以相信的想法
Science is full of ideas that seem hard to believe.

469
00:24:53,880 --> 00:24:55,770
来看量子力学
Take quantum mechanics.

470
00:24:55,880 --> 00:24:59,540
在这个亚原子的陌生世界里
In this strange world of subatomic physics,

471
00:24:59,650 --> 00:25:03,210
粒子可以同时身处两地…
a particle can be in two places at once...

472
00:25:03,330 --> 00:25:05,160
直到我们看到它
Until we look at it.

473
00:25:08,200 --> 00:25:10,290
多数物理学家会告诉你
Most physicists will tell you

474
00:25:10,400 --> 00:25:13,920
粒子的归宿之地就是掷骰子
where the particle ends up is just a roll of the dice.

475
00:25:14,040 --> 00:25:16,390
不过有另一个理论
But there's another theory.

476
00:25:16,500 --> 00:25:18,090
我的心智
My conscious mind

477
00:25:18,210 --> 00:25:22,030
可能受到这个亚原子世界的控制
could be controlling this subatomic world.

478
00:25:22,140 --> 00:25:23,900
第六感
And the sixth sense

479
00:25:24,010 --> 00:25:27,540
可能就是产生宇宙时间的东西
could be what makes the universe tick.

480
00:25:27,650 --> 00:25:32,510
加来道雄是个理论物理学家
Michio Kaku is a theoretical physicist.

481
00:25:32,620 --> 00:25:34,740
作为弦理论的先驱
As a pioneer of string theory,

482
00:25:34,860 --> 00:25:38,750
该理论认为世界实际上是九维的
which proposes the world is actually nine-dimensional,

483
00:25:38,860 --> 00:25:42,380
他认为科学家需要
he believes scientists need to keep an open mind

484
00:25:42,500 --> 00:25:44,090
对第六感保持开放的心态
about the sixth sense,

485
00:25:44,200 --> 00:25:47,820
无论它听上去有多怪异
no matter how strange it may sound.

486
00:25:47,940 --> 00:25:51,060
我们物理学家是保守的革命家
We physicists are conservative revolutionaries

487
00:25:51,170 --> 00:25:53,090
一定意义上 我们得直面
in the sense that we have to be open

488
00:25:53,210 --> 00:25:55,400
各种疯狂 怪异的现象
to all sorts of crazy,bizarre phenomenon.

489
00:25:55,510 --> 00:25:56,600
谁会想到
Who would have thought

490
00:25:56,710 --> 00:25:59,000
有所谓的放射性的东西呢？
that there's something called radioactivity?

491
00:25:59,110 --> 00:26:01,870
谁会想到我们会有量子力呢？
Who would have thought that we would have quantum forces?

492
00:26:01,980 --> 00:26:05,300
所以我们得直面这些东西
So we have to be open to these things.

493
00:26:05,420 --> 00:26:08,770
空前最成功的物理理论
The most successful physical theory of all time

494
00:26:08,890 --> 00:26:12,540
就叫做量子力学 原子的理论
is called quantum mechanics,the theory of the atom,

495
00:26:12,660 --> 00:26:15,680
因为它的基础概念就是概率
because it's based on the idea of probabilities,

496
00:26:15,790 --> 00:26:18,820
你实际上并不知道电子在哪里
that you don't really know where an electron is.

497
00:26:18,930 --> 00:26:21,490
电子的存在 某种意义上
And electrons can exist,in some sense,

498
00:26:21,600 --> 00:26:23,960
可以同时有多种状态
in multiple states at the same time.

499
00:26:24,070 --> 00:26:27,090
弗里曼：亚原子粒子的不确定性
The fuzzy nature of subatomic particles

500
00:26:27,210 --> 00:26:32,300
或许就提供了一个途径来解释第六感
might just provide a way to explain the sixth sense.

501
00:26:32,410 --> 00:26:33,630
薛定谔
Erwin Schrodinger,

502
00:26:33,750 --> 00:26:36,540
量子力学的奠基人之一
one of the founders of quantum mechanics,

503
00:26:36,650 --> 00:26:39,540
设计了一个思想实验来阐明
designed a thought experiment to drive home

504
00:26:39,650 --> 00:26:43,280
其理论的奇怪规则
the strange rules of his theory.

505
00:26:43,390 --> 00:26:49,090
比方说我们将一只猫和一瓶毒药放在一个盒子里
Let's say we put a cat and a vial of poison in a box.

506
00:26:50,730 --> 00:26:54,650
我们放入一个放射性铀原子
We add an atom of radioactive uranium

507
00:26:54,770 --> 00:26:56,960
和一个盖革计数器
and a geiger counter.

508
00:26:57,070 --> 00:26:59,830
如果铀原子发生衰变 它就会启动盖革计数器
If the uranium decays,it sets off the geiger counter,

509
00:26:59,940 --> 00:27:04,640
于是就释放出毒药 默默地毒死小猫
which then releases the poison and silently kills the cat.

510
00:27:05,980 --> 00:27:07,830
在我们打开盒子观察之前
Before we open the box and look,

511
00:27:07,950 --> 00:27:11,610
我们其实无法得知铀衰变与否
we can't actually know whether the uranium has decayed or not

512
00:27:11,720 --> 00:27:13,940
因为放射性衰变
since radioactive decay

513
00:27:14,050 --> 00:27:19,310
是一个概率量子事件
is a probabilistic quantum event.

514
00:27:19,430 --> 00:27:20,750
问题来了
Here's the question.

515
00:27:20,860 --> 00:27:22,480
猫是死是活呢？
Is the cat dead or alive?

516
00:27:22,600 --> 00:27:25,950
这个 根据量子力学
Well,according to quantum mechanics,

517
00:27:26,070 --> 00:27:29,090
猫既没死也没活着
the cat is neither dead nor alive

518
00:27:29,200 --> 00:27:31,730
而是这两种形态并存
but the sum of the two states.

519
00:27:31,840 --> 00:27:34,700
那好 此时 你会说 别胡说八道了
Well,at that point,you say,"Well,that's nonsense.

520
00:27:34,810 --> 00:27:36,030
荒谬之极
"That's preposterous.

521
00:27:36,140 --> 00:27:38,900
你怎么可能生死并存呢？
"How can you be both dead and alive simultaneously?"

522
00:27:39,010 --> 00:27:42,440
弗里曼：薛定谔的猫本来是表明
Schrodinger's cat was supposed to show

523
00:27:42,550 --> 00:27:45,540
这个宇宙间没有什么是一定的
that nothing in this universe is certain

524
00:27:45,650 --> 00:27:48,240
直到有人进行度量
until someone makes a measurement.

525
00:27:48,360 --> 00:27:51,410
不过量子力学的另一位先驱
But another pioneer of quantum mechanics,

526
00:27:51,530 --> 00:27:53,920
尤金.威格纳 认为这能够告诉我们
Eugene Wigner,believed it could teach us

527
00:27:54,030 --> 00:27:56,950
其它关于宇宙运作的东西 -
something else about the working of the universe --

528
00:27:57,070 --> 00:28:01,420
即意识控制一切
that consciousness controls everything.

529
00:28:01,540 --> 00:28:07,030
道来：威格纳称 让我们更进一步
Wigner said,"Let's take it one step farther.

530
00:28:07,140 --> 00:28:09,370
如果我 作为人类 观察那只猫
"If I,a human being,looks at the cat,

