00:37:05,260 --> 00:37:08,850
在上世纪50年代 天才物理学家理查德.费曼
In the 1950s,genius physicist Richard Feynman

705
00:37:08,970 --> 00:37:11,960
认识到超前波方案
realized that advanced wave solutions

706
00:37:12,070 --> 00:37:14,430
实际上是数学上的线索
were actually mathematical clues

707
00:37:14,540 --> 00:37:18,260
表示存在有新的物质形式 - 反物质
that a new form of matter existed -- antimatter.

708
00:37:18,380 --> 00:37:19,570
嗯
Hmm.

709
00:37:19,680 --> 00:37:24,840
物质貌似在时间上往后走
What looks like matter traveling backwards in time

710
00:37:24,950 --> 00:37:29,810
实际上是反物质完全正常的行事
is actually antimatter acting perfectly normal.

711
00:37:29,920 --> 00:37:33,350
道来：物质在时间上倒行
Matter going backwards in time

712
00:37:33,460 --> 00:37:37,880
等同于反物质在时间上超前
is the same as antimatter going forwards in time.

713
00:37:38,000 --> 00:37:40,190
我们认为那或许 只是或许
We thought that maybe,just maybe,

714
00:37:40,300 --> 00:37:42,760
有可能能够看到未来
it might be possible to see the future,

715
00:37:42,870 --> 00:37:46,190
在现在与我们的子孙后代打交道
communicate with our descendents from the present time.

716
00:37:46,300 --> 00:37:48,800
不过且听费曼的 "没这回事"
But here comes Feynman,who says,"no."

717
00:37:51,240 --> 00:37:53,870
弗里曼：费曼以此项研究获得了诺贝尔大奖
Feynman won a nobel prize for this work.

718
00:37:53,980 --> 00:37:57,400
但是迪安.雷丁并不认为超前波
But Dean Radin isn't convinced that advanced waves

719
00:37:57,520 --> 00:38:00,440
在时间上的倒行
rippling backwards in time from the future

720
00:38:00,550 --> 00:38:04,310
可以被一笔勾销
can be written off entirely.

721
00:38:04,420 --> 00:38:05,610
雷丁：在现在物理学里
In modern physics,

722
00:38:05,730 --> 00:38:07,720
我们现在至少有了一个可信的论据
now we at least have a plausibility argument,

723
00:38:07,830 --> 00:38:10,200
我们可以不再说现实世界
where we can no longer say that the physical world

724
00:38:10,310 --> 00:38:11,310
对此无能为力
makes it impossible.

725
00:38:11,420 --> 00:38:12,690
我们知道它是有可能的
We know that it is possible.

726
00:38:12,800 --> 00:38:14,220
所以现在的挑战是说
So the challenge now is to say,

727
00:38:14,340 --> 00:38:16,430
啊 我们如何才能填补这个缺失？
"Well,how do we connect this missing gap?"

728
00:38:16,540 --> 00:38:20,800
弗里曼：理论物理学的进展是华山一条路
Advances in theoretical physics are one way.

729
00:38:20,910 --> 00:38:22,900
但是还有别的路 -
But there is another --

730
00:38:23,010 --> 00:38:26,400
更多的证据
more evidence.

731
00:38:26,510 --> 00:38:29,100
这个研究者可能就是那个人
This researcher could be the man

732
00:38:29,220 --> 00:38:31,570
他最终让世界明白
who finally convinces the world

733
00:38:31,690 --> 00:38:35,020
第六感是真实的
that the sixth sense is real.

734
00:38:37,960 --> 00:38:40,150
一个多世纪以来
Scientists have been searching for evidence

735
00:38:40,270 --> 00:38:43,340
科学家一直在寻找第六感的证据
of the sixth sense for well over a century.

736
00:38:43,800 --> 00:38:45,620
如果它存在
If it exists,

737
00:38:45,740 --> 00:38:48,660
它不可能强如其它五个感官
it can't be as strong as the other five senses.

738
00:38:48,770 --> 00:38:51,800
否则 我们就不会对此还在争论不休了
Otherwise,we wouldn't still be arguing about it.

739
00:38:51,910 --> 00:38:55,870
但是若我们能够证明第六感是真实的
But if we can prove that the sixth sense is real,

740
00:38:55,980 --> 00:38:58,370
也就不在乎它有多弱了
it won't matter how weak it is.

741
00:38:58,480 --> 00:39:01,870
它将会把现代科学彻底颠覆了
It would turn modern science on its head.

742
00:39:01,990 --> 00:39:06,110
达里尔.本有一个稳定而成功的职业
Daryl Bem has had a long and successful career

743
00:39:06,230 --> 00:39:10,750
是康奈尔大学心理学教授
as a Professor of Psychology at Cornell University.

744
00:39:10,860 --> 00:39:15,850
现在他也将自己的重点转向了第六感
Now he,too,has turned his focus to the sixth sense.

745
00:39:15,970 --> 00:39:20,590
我愿意致力于先知或预感
I wanted to do work on precognition or premonition

746
00:39:20,700 --> 00:39:22,830
因为它就是不可思议
because it just boggles the mind

747
00:39:22,940 --> 00:39:26,130
未来居然可以影响过去
to think that the future can affect the past.

748
00:39:26,240 --> 00:39:30,730
弗里曼：达里尔花了8年时间
Daryl has spent the last eight years

749
00:39:30,850 --> 00:39:33,470
测试这个基本问题
testing this very question.

750
00:39:33,580 --> 00:39:35,640
一个人面前是两块窗帘
A person is shown two curtains

751
00:39:35,750 --> 00:39:39,720
被告知 一块窗帘背后会是一幅画
and are told that behind one of the curtains will be a picture

752
00:39:39,830 --> 00:39:41,880
而另一块窗帘背后是一片空白的墙面
and behind the other is a blank wall.

753
00:39:41,990 --> 00:39:44,450
他们的任务是挑选出
And their task is to pick the curtain

754
00:39:44,560 --> 00:39:47,120
背后有画的窗帘
that has the picture behind it.

755
00:39:47,410 --> 00:39:49,530
弗里曼：和迪安.雷丁一样
Just like Dean Radin,

756
00:39:49,650 --> 00:39:53,070
达里尔想看看人们是否能预见
Daryl is trying to see whether people can anticipate

757
00:39:53,180 --> 00:39:54,840
未来的事件
future events.

758
00:39:54,950 --> 00:39:56,910
本：电脑在等待 直到他们做出选择
The computer waits until they've made their selection,

759
00:39:57,020 --> 00:40:00,340
没有看到他们有任何作弊
and then,without cheating by looking at what they did,

760
00:40:00,460 --> 00:40:02,440
就是抛硬币
it flips a coin.

761
00:40:02,560 --> 00:40:06,580
弗里曼：大部分时间 他们的成功率是50对50
Most of the time,their success rate is 50/50.

762
00:40:06,700 --> 00:40:10,090
也就是说 他们在猜
In other words,they're guessing.

763
00:40:10,200 --> 00:40:13,790
不过一旦且唯有当
But when and only when

764
00:40:13,900 --> 00:40:15,690
电脑出现色情画面时
the computer shows erotic images,

765
00:40:15,800 --> 00:40:18,190
试验者能够预测到窗帘后面的东西
subjects can predict what's behind the curtain

766
00:40:18,310 --> 00:40:21,200
53%的比例 -
53% of the time --

767
00:40:21,310 --> 00:40:24,000
一个不大但统计意义重大的
a small but statistically significant

768
00:40:24,110 --> 00:40:25,500
概率跳动
beating of the odds.

769
00:40:25,610 --> 00:40:29,530
达里尔认为这种觉察
Daryl believes this ability to sense erotic opportunities

770
00:40:29,650 --> 00:40:30,650
未来的色情机会的能力
in the future

771
00:40:30,760 --> 00:40:33,410
已经发展了有数百万年
has developed over millions of years.

772
00:40:33,520 --> 00:40:37,250
它是进化形成的
It was shaped by evolution to give individuals an edge

773
00:40:37,360 --> 00:40:38,580
赋予了人找到配偶的优势
in finding mates.

774
00:40:38,690 --> 00:40:42,350
进化凭借着繁衍的优势 -
Evolution rides on reproductive advantage --

775
00:40:42,460 --> 00:40:46,850
寻求和把握异性机会的能力
the ability to seek out and have sexual opportunities.

776
00:40:46,970 --> 00:40:49,790
所以这就让进化到
So it makes sense evolutionarily

777
00:40:49,900 --> 00:40:53,800
觉得能预测之类的意识
to think that precognition or something like it

778
00:40:53,910 --> 00:40:57,570
能定会提供繁衍优势
would certainly serve reproductive advantage

779
00:40:57,680 --> 00:40:59,570
和生存优势
and survival advantage.

780
00:40:59,680 --> 00:41:02,970
弗里曼：若是他是对的
If he's right,

781
00:41:03,090 --> 00:41:06,810
那达里尔就揭示了人性中
Daryl has revealed a completely unexpected aspect

782
00:41:06,920 --> 00:41:08,210
完全出乎意料的一面
of human nature.

783
00:41:08,330 --> 00:41:12,120
时间或许并不会往一个方向一帆风顺地流逝
Time may not flow neatly in one direction.

784
00:41:12,230 --> 00:41:15,990
人类 作为进化的幸运儿
And humans,being evolutionary survivors,

785
00:41:16,100 --> 00:41:20,060
已经学会了利用自己的优势
have learned to use that to their advantage.

786
00:41:20,170 --> 00:41:23,430
本：我将其称之为感受未来
I call it "Feeling the future"

787
00:41:23,540 --> 00:41:25,400
因为它试图进入未来
because it tries to get in the fact

788
00:41:25,510 --> 00:41:27,300
未来不仅能影响
that the future is able to affect

789
00:41:27,410 --> 00:41:30,100
你的思想 认识 还有你的情感
both your thoughts -- cognition -- and your emotions.

790
00:41:30,220 --> 00:41:33,040
弗里曼：当它发表在
When it was published

791
00:41:33,150 --> 00:41:37,780
《个性与社会心理学杂志》后
in the Journal of Personality and Social Psychology,

792
00:41:37,890 --> 00:41:40,550
达里尔的文章引起了全世界的关注
Daryl's article caught worldwide attention.

793
00:41:40,660 --> 00:41:45,180
第六感研究 长期处在科学的边缘
Sixth-sense research,long on the fringes of science,

794
00:41:45,200 --> 00:41:49,590
正逐渐成为主流
is moving ever closer to the mainstream.

795
00:41:49,700 --> 00:41:51,790
第六感那样的玩意无处不在
There's more sixth-sense stuff around

796
00:41:51,900 --> 00:41:54,160
超出了我们可能愿意接受的程度
than we are maybe willing to acknowledge

797
00:41:54,270 --> 00:41:57,200
因为我们持续不断处理的信息
because we are processing much more information

798
00:41:57,310 --> 00:41:59,670
远超出了我们所觉察到的
on a continuous basis than we are aware of.

799
00:41:59,780 --> 00:42:01,670
伯辛格：它显然是物质的
It's clearly physical,

800
00:42:01,780 --> 00:42:03,840
它受制于少量的能量
it's tied to small amounts of energy,

801
00:42:03,950 --> 00:42:06,200
它告诉我们 我们与我们
and it tells us that there's a connection

802
00:42:06,320 --> 00:42:08,240
周围的世界存在着关联
between us and our world around us

803
00:42:08,350 --> 00:42:09,910
那是我们尚未搞明白
that we haven't previously fathomed.

804
00:42:10,020 --> 00:42:12,780
本：我们已经到了我们能够看到
We're at the point where we can show

805
00:42:12,890 --> 00:42:14,880
我们有了异常的发现
that we have anomalous findings.

806
00:42:14,990 --> 00:42:16,580
异常对我们意味着什么呢？
And what do we mean by anomalous?

807
00:42:16,700 --> 00:42:19,050
它意味着它并不适合目前
It means it doesn't fit into the current structure

808
00:42:19,170 --> 00:42:23,220
我们如何去概念化实际规律的结构
of how we conceptualize physical reality.

809
00:42:23,340 --> 00:42:24,890
我们走到了知识的边缘
We're looking at the edge of what's known.

810
00:42:25,010 --> 00:42:27,360
雷丁：我觉得我们能够满怀信心地说
I think we can say with high confidence

811
00:42:27,470 --> 00:42:29,760
在心里现象的领域里
that in the realm of psychic phenomena,

812
00:42:29,880 --> 00:42:31,670
有趣的事情正在发生
something interesting is happening.

813
00:42:31,780 --> 00:42:35,640
弗里曼：有第六感么？
Is there a sixth sense?

814
00:42:35,750 --> 00:42:39,340
那甚至都不是一个提出的合适的问题
That's not even the right question to ask anymore.

815
00:42:39,450 --> 00:42:42,840
主流脑研究已经发现了
Mainstream brain research has already uncovered

816
00:42:42,960 --> 00:42:45,650
以前从不知晓的感知途径
previously unknown sensory pathways.

817
00:42:45,760 --> 00:42:49,450
但不管我们的思想是否能够融入全球意识
But whether our thoughts can join a global mind

818
00:42:49,560 --> 00:42:52,450
或我们是否能够感觉未来
or whether we can sense the future,

819
00:42:52,570 --> 00:42:55,920
我们至今只有零星的证据
we only have fragments of evidence so far.

820
00:42:56,040 --> 00:42:58,990
最终 我们会找到答案的
In the end,we will find the answers

821
00:42:59,110 --> 00:43:01,330
因为它们全都…
because they're all...

822
00:43:01,440 --> 00:43:02,650
在这里
Right here.

823
00:43:05,110 --> 00:43:06,110
-- 感谢观赏 --

